  "id": "COMPOUND:28794 - PROTEIN:5805",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between Michaolide J and SCCH-26 through a series of target interactions. Michaolide J is implicated as a target of Thioredoxin, mitochondrial, which in turn is targeted by Yuanhunine and Cyclizidine, both of which also target SCCH-26. This indicates that Michaolide J may exert its biological effect via a pathway involving Thioredoxin, mitochondrial, and ultimately SCCH-26. The consistent scores across the three paths suggest a robust, though indirect, connection between Michaolide J and SCCH-26, likely mediated through the Thioredoxin family of proteins. The overlapping targets and the shared downstream effect on SCCH-26 imply a possible mechanism of action that involves the modulation of mitochondrial thioredoxin, which could influence cellular processes in the SCCH-26 cell line. The integration of these pathways highlights the role of Thioredoxin in linking Michaolide J to SCCH-26, though the exact molecular mechanism remains to be elucidated.",
